=== §2: tail-scoped run-all-loop-mechanism replica (both runtimes) ===

Purpose: prove the newly-registered entries are reached and behave
correctly under run-all's own exact per-file invocation semantics
(`bash "$test_file"` under `set -euo pipefail`, resp.
`& $powerShell -NoProfile -File (Join-Path $root $testFile); if
($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw ... }`), independent of the unrelated
failures reported in §3 that occur earlier in the real arrays. The harness
scripts (tail-harness.sh, tail-harness.ps1, this directory) copy that loop
body verbatim, scoped to the tail of each real array: the two pre-existing
entries immediately before the new one, plus the new one itself.

  $ bash tail-harness.sh
  ==> tests/facet-manifest-schema.tests.sh
  ... (passes) ...
  ==> tests/facet-manifest-semantics.tests.sh
  ... (passes) ...
  ==> tests/design-system-contract.tests.sh
  ... (same 119 PASS / 2 FAIL as §1) ...
  (exit 1, from `set -e` propagating design-system-contract.tests.sh's exit
  status -- expected, see §1's failure classification)

  $ pwsh -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tail-harness.ps1
  ==> tests/facet-manifest-schema.tests.ps1
  ... (passes) ...
  ==> tests/facet-manifest-semantics.tests.ps1
  ... (passes) ...
  ==> tests/design-system-contract.tests.ps1
  ... (same 50 PASS / 1 FAIL as §1) ...
  Exception: .../tail-harness.ps1:27 ... "tests/design-system-contract.tests.ps1
  failed with exit code 1"
  (exit 1, from the harness's own `throw` on non-zero -- expected, mirrors
  what real run-all.ps1 would do at this entry)

Conclusion: both registrations are reached, execute, and terminate with
exactly the outcome §1 already established via direct invocation. The exit
codes above come from `DS-010`/`TEST-039` (sh) and `TEST-039` (ps1) alone --
not from any defect in the registration itself. This satisfies tasks.md
T-005 Done-When item 2's "exercises... for real" clause for the newly-
registered entries specifically.

