`pwsh ... run-all.ps1` processes concurrently active in this same shared
worktree from other agent sessions (timestamps 9:20PM-9:46PM, several
distinct zsh parent PIDs with distinct `CODEX_COMPANION_SESSION_ID` values)
-- this is the "shared-worktree concurrent-agent hazard" pattern.

--- run-all.ps1 ---

Completed within this task's session. Halted at `tests/cross-model.tests.ps1`
(array position ~24 of 32, entered via `throw "$testFile failed with exit
code $LASTEXITCODE"` at run-all.ps1:51) with "Results: 48 passed, 14 failed"
-- 14 timing/wall-clock-budget assertions (TEST-003 gemini timeout,
TEST-004(a)/(c) gpt+gemini near-boundary and wall-clock-bound checks,
elapsed_ms measurements of ~3800-5300ms). Re-ran `cross-model.tests.ps1` in
isolation (untouched by this task, no other file before it in the array
touched either): reproduced the identical 14-failure pattern
(48 passed / 14 failed) at that point in time. This is upstream of, and
unrelated to, `tests/design-system-contract.tests.ps1` (last entry) --
never reached in this run. Root cause: wall-clock budgets tuned for an
unloaded machine, exceeded under the concurrent-session CPU contention
described above -- an environmental condition, not a defect in this task's
one-line addition to a 32-entry array positioned after it.

--- run-all.sh ---

Completed within this task's session (after several minutes, under the same
contention). Halted at `tests/prepare-panelist.tests.sh` (array position 7
of 65, `set -euo pipefail` propagating that file's own non-zero exit) with
"Results: 48 passed, 3 failed" -- "FAIL: PP-001a: no consent should exit
non-zero, got 0", "FAIL: PP-001b: output file must NOT be created without
consent", "FAIL: PP-001c: error message should mention 'consent', got:
<hash>". PP-001 asserts fail-closed behaviour when *neither* a tasks.md flag
*nor* `SDD_SUDO` grants consent -- a precondition about ambient environment
state, not this suite's own logic. This shared worktree's scratchpad already
contains an `enable-sdd-sudo.sh` script (evidence a concurrent session in
this same environment exercises the `SDD_SUDO` consent path), consistent
with ambient `SDD_SUDO` state from a concurrent session causing PP-001's
